hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"262","Yunus bin Abdul Ala told us, Abdullah bin Wahb bin Muslim told us that Malik told him, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al Qasim, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, may God Almighty be pleased with her, that she said: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on some of his travels, until When we were in Al-Baida or in Dhat Al-Jaysh, a contract with me was cut off, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed to contact him, and the people stayed with him. They were not on water, and they had no water with them, so the people came to Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God Almighty be pleased with him, and they said: Don’t you see what Aisha has done? She stayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with the people, but they were not on water, and they had no water, so Abu Bakr and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. He leaned over and laid his head on my thigh and fell asleep.” He mentioned the hadith in its entirety."
